Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Propagators", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.948188002344557*^9, 
  3.9481880108612843`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"040bf299-f276-4bd8-86cd-\
f7e1c9892191"],

Cell["\<\
We define 13 propagators of the form k^2-m^2 (where m might be zero), \
labelled P1-P13. Each diagram needs 7 propagators. Unless certain propagators \
are repeated, we need 5 for denominators and 2 extra needed to form a \
linearly independent basis to solve for all scalar products. Note we also \
have 2 equations of motion, allowing us to solve for 9 unknowns (in addition \
we define q.q=q2).

These propagators and the choices of propagators for each diagram family are \
defined in the sbcc document. Below, we solve for all the scalar products in \
each family in terms of the correct propagators.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.94825770472606*^9, 
  3.948258073386806*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a48283bd-8fea-4b88-aa77-\
2fa3656febb2"],

